\ Fixture exercised by `make aot-asm-name-check` to verify that AOT-emitted C carries `asm("...")`
\ declaration attributes on the forward declarations of user-defined words, prelude words,
\ compiled quotation bodies, and generated words, and that the resulting linker symbols carry the
\ same names.
\
\ Word names below intentionally include `?`, `-`, and `>` so the verbatim-preservation policy
\ is observable in both the saved C source and the binary's symbol table.

parse-json?: ( -- ) [ "ok" print-line ] ;
>foo: ( -- ) [ "in" print-line ] ;

\ The `if` arms below are compiled quotation literals. Each gets a separate emitted C function whose
\ symbol is named `pick-quot/quot@<line>:<col>` -- the `<line>:<col>` is the position of the opening
\ `[`. The two arms must produce distinct asm-names; they sit on separate source lines, so the line
\ part distinguishes them.
pick-quot: ( ? -- ) [
  [ "yes" print-line ]
  [ "no" print-line ]
  if
] ;

\ Twin one-line siblings, distinguishable only by column within the same source line. This
\ single-line case exercises true column-based disambiguation; the multi-line `pick-quot` case
\ above exercises source-accurate columns on indented continuation lines.
flip: ( ? -- ) [ [ "lo" print-line ] [ "hi" print-line ] if ] ;

\ A struct with a uniquely-named field exercises the devirtualized field-accessor path: the dispatch
\ table holds a single method for `serial>>`, so AOT compiles the accessor body into its own C function
\ whose symbol is qualified with the struct name (`person/serial>>`). The field name must stay unique
\ across the always-loaded prelude; `id` would collide with the prelude's `constraint-info` record and
\ make `serial>>`'s generic polymorphic, forcing the not-yet-supported AOT runtime-dispatch path.
person: struct{ serial } ;

\ An enum exercises the word-level provenance path: the aggregate predicate `status?` is emitted as
\ `status/status?` so it does not collide with other aggregate predicates spelled `status?`.
status: enum{
  active: unit
  inactive: unit
} ;

parse-json?
>foo
t pick-quot
f pick-quot
t flip
f flip
42 make-person serial>> .
status:active status? .
